SWEET nav15 (patch 0259, T-18b3, G-10b-nav; log only, no register or memory write outside the patch's own statics): the THRWAIT sampler (patch 0249/0250) also samples the Preferences process (third entry next to backboardd and SpringBoard) and prints every entry of the current Preferences pid once per second as `SWEET THRWAIT: pref pid P tid T idx I hint H ev E pc PC lr LR n N`, outside the 24-row top list that would cut it. Why: nav14 rep 2 (20261108T120635Z-gputest-nav14): the About gate was satisfied (68 swaps, flat 504 ms) and three About taps gave 0 swaps; the sampler named no Preferences thread, so a dead About cannot be told from a tap that reached an idle app versus a tap that never reached it.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_thrwait.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_thrwait.c
index e16ebda..1449b7d 100644
